MID_SCXX_08_01_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_001: This is the place. From the outside, it's your everyday\nrun-down building.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_002: But if you look close, you'll see a cleverly disguised\nentrance to an underground area.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_003: Hmm... I'm not really seeing it, even though you're\ntrying to point it out.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_004: You're saying it's an entrance to an underground\narea, but I just see a wall.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_005: An abandoned building? I had hoped for more from\nthis summons.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_006: Yet there might be something inside. Very well, let\nus enter.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_007: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_008: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_009: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_010: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_070: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_071: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_072: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_011: We're not quite ready to head inside. There's still\none person who's yet to join us.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_012: You did not mention adding another party to this\nexpedition. I assumed it was only us.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_013: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_014: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_015: My apologies if I've kept you waiting.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_016: I'm grateful for your help in this matter. I can breathe\neasier knowing you're with us.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_017: Wait. By "one person," do you mean Solel?
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_018: But why are you trying to sneak into this place?
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_019: Divine Sovereign... What business have you in\nthis place?
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_020: Well, no matter. I am eager to see what you are\ncapable of.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_021: The Divine Sovereign?! Why would someone of your\nstature be here?
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_022: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_023: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_024: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_025: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_026: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_027: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_028: My motives must remain guarded. Suffice to say\nI have reason to see to this personally.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_029: Tell no one I was here, please.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_030: Well, with that settled, I'll explain as much as I can\nwithout going over the line.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_031: A certain organization has been secretly gathering\norichalcum from all over Dagda.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_032: Our investigation showed that this orichalcum has\nbeen flowing into Dagsion.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_033: They've been hiding it in caches all over the city.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_034: Thanks to Anna, we have a strong suspicion that\nthis is one of those caches.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_035: You may already be aware, but it's a serious crime\nto trade in orichalcum without temple permission.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_036: But I felt I should confirm the rumors for myself\nbefore mobilizing the temples to act.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_037: I see... So the Order of Mithras is involved in\nthis, eh?
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_038: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_039: Lord Solel, we haven't seen any sign of lookouts.\nLet's sneak in and find out what they're hiding.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_040: Oh, wow. This is incredible. Look at the shiny bars\npiled way up high.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_041: As dull within as without.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_042: I cannot believe my eyes... This amount of the metal\nis inconceivable.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_043: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_044: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_045: You're kidding me. Just how much orichalcum have\nthey been smuggling?!
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_046: For them to have this much stockpiled without my\nknowing is beyond the pale.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_047: What would Magistra Raksha need with it all?
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_048: It's more than I've ever seen. Surely no one would\nmiss a bar or two...
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_049: Kidding, kidding! Hm? Did something just brush\nmy foot?
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_050: *squeak*
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_051: A-ah... AAAH!
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_052: Anna?! What's the matter?
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_053: A-a mouse! A HUGE mouse! I-I-I can't stand them!
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_054: Who treads within this vault? You are trespassing!
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_055: No one who has seen what we store here can be\nallowed to live, no matter who—
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_056: L-Lord Solel?! Wh-what are you doing here?
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_057: I wondered the same of you, Vinicius. Don't tell me\nyou're part of the Order of Mithras too.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_058: It's dismaying to see that their tendrils reach so deep\ninto the empire.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_059: Lord Solel, I am so sorry. It's my fault they found us.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_060: We cannot allow Magistra Raksha to learn of our\nactions today.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_061: Apprehend everyone here. Do not let a single\none escape.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_062: Got it. I can handle this.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_063: Hah. I would have it no other way!
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_064: Very well. I will capture them as you ask.
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_065: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_066: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_067: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_068: 
MID_SCXX_08_01_m01_069: Alrighty! Let's hit them hard and fast!
MID_SCXX_08_02_m01: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m01_001: I am very disappointed, Vinicius. You were a\ntrusted advisor of mine.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m01_002: And yet you have betrayed me for them... I will\ndemand a full account of your reasoning later.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m01_003: Comply, and I will guarantee your safety. Do we\nhave an agreement?
MID_SCXX_08_02_m13: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m01_004: Huh?! There's no way the Divine Sovereign would\nstoop to coming here.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m01_005: This must be some villain pretending to be him!\nFor your insolence, I'll slay you where you stand.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m02: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m02_001: Lord Solel thought highly enough of your cautious\nnature that you were known as the Lead Statue.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m02_002: And now you have the gall to backstab him? This is\na story I've got to hear.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m03: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m03_001: On pain of death, I shall prevent you from interfering\nwith Magistra Raksha's plans!
MID_SCXX_08_02_m03_002: What has gotten into you? Where does this loyalty\nto her come from?
MID_SCXX_08_02_m04: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m04_001: You surprised me, Lord Solel. I had no idea you\nwere so strong.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m04_002: You are quite impressive yourself. I can tell you've\nbeen tutored by a vulkan.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m04_003: Pop taught me how to fight. It's kinda complicated,\nbut he's my dad, and I'm proud of him.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m04_004: Hm. That reminds me, your wish was...
MID_SCXX_08_02_m04_005: Right. That's why I'm gonna fight my hardest and\nwin the games.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m04_006: Stand strong, Cai. Only the force of your will can\nopen the path you seek.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m05: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m05_001: Your skill exceeds my expectations. I crave a duel,\none day.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m05_002: It has been too long since I took up this spear. But I\nsee time has not dulled my skills.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m05_003: The way you wield it... It is familiar to me, somehow.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m05_004: I believe this is the first time I've wielded my spear\nbefore you. Perhaps you're thinking of someone else?
MID_SCXX_08_02_m06: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m06_001: I had not taken you for such a capable warrior,\nDivine Sovereign.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m06_002: It has been too long since I took up this spear.\nFortunately, time has not dulled my skills.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m06_003: I apologize for involving you in this, Queen\nTheodora. But there are few I'd rather fight beside.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m06_004: The same is true for me. Now, let us vanquish this\nrabble quickly.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m07: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m07_001: I wasn't expecting you to fight alongside us—or to be\nso skilled in combat, frankly.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m07_002: Where did you learn to wield a spear so well? I'm not\nvery familiar with the world of gods.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m07_003: It was during my time at the paradise called Zanado\nin Fódlan, before I came here to Dagda.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m07_004: I learned it from a Founder named Ildánach, who is\nrenowned among our kind as a master of the spear.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m07_005: I see. So gods, too, have mentors. I wouldn't have\nthought that.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m07_006: There may be less difference between gods and\nhumans than you would believe.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m08: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m08_001: Impressive skills, Uncle! The stories don't do\nyou justice!
MID_SCXX_08_02_m08_002: I find it comforting to have a nephew like you\nfighting alongside me.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m08_003: And as your nephew, maybe I could keep, let's say...\n10 percent of that orichalcum?
MID_SCXX_08_02_m08_004: Alas, no. There are strict protocols governing the\norichalcum trade.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m08_005: You're more by the book than I imagined. Still, it\nwas worth a shot!
MID_SCXX_08_02_m09: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m09_001: I was surprised to see you here, Lord Solel.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m09_002: You know me as Divine Sovereign, but I once took\nthis spear in hand to survey the breadth of Dagda.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m09_003: It was a dangerous journey. I faced many ruthless\ncreatures in my travels.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m09_004: That was also the journey on which I met my wife,\nYu Phas.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m09_005: What a turn of events... That must be a lovely story.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m09_006: I'd like to hear all about that sometime, if you\nwouldn't mind.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m09_007: Very well... If you wish to hear it, I see no harm in\nrecounting it to you.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m10: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m10_001: You're surprisingly practiced on the battlefield,\nDivine Sovereign.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m10_002: You're no less impressive. Were those techniques\npassed down among the People of the White Egg?
MID_SCXX_08_02_m10_003: Yes. It is a martial art taught for many generations\nin my village. I learned it from my master.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m10_004: How strange it is to fight side by side with someone\nof the White Egg.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m10_005: I somehow feel that I could trust you with my life.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m10_006: And I you, Divine Sovereign. Let us put an end to\nthis trouble together.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11_001: What is Vinicius thinking, letting these things\nloose underground?!
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11_002: That's funny, coming from someone who rides\nan elephant.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11_003: Strange for you to say so.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11_004: I will not dispute the point, but...that elephant of\nyours is no less risky.
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11_005: 
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11_006: 
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11_007: 
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11_008: 
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11_009: Hey, don't lump me in with that reckless dolt!
MID_SCXX_08_02_m11_010: Do you have any idea how much concentration it\ntakes to handle an elephant in this tight space?!
MID_SCXX_08_02_m12: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_02_m12_001: Grrraaah!
MID_SCXX_08_02_m12_002: No! S-stop! You'll bring the whole place down around\nour ears!
MID_SCXX_08_02_m12_003: Oh dear. The ceiling is about to collapse. Everyone,\nhurry and get above ground!
MID_SCXX_08_e01: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e01_001: Step forth, my powerful servant! Crush all those who\nwould stand in our way!
MID_SCXX_08_e02: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e02_001: He has summoned a giant?! But how? He does not\npossess such raw power.
MID_SCXX_08_e04: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e04_001: Lord Solel, please stay back! I shall swiftly handle\nthis with the aid of my vicious war elephant!
MID_SCXX_08_e03: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e03_001: What is this? Not even so much as a scratch?!\nIndeed, this is no ordinary giant!
MID_SCXX_08_e03_002: So this is the true scope of their power... Anna,\nleave this to me.
MID_SCXX_08_e05: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e05_001: Incredible... Well done, Lord Solel! We shall follow\nyour lead!
MID_SCXX_08_e06: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e06_001: How vexing. I see now this requires all the power\nbestowed upon me. Come forth again, my servant!
MID_SCXX_08_e09: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e09_001: He refuses to learn his lesson yet?! No...there is\nsomething more ominous about this new giant!
MID_SCXX_08_e10: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e10_001: Such strength... It seems to be enhanced by some\npower its predecessor lacked.
MID_SCXX_08_e10_002: I see now! The nearby {SetColor=Gold}orichalcum piles {SetColor=Default}are\namplifying the giant's strength!
MID_SCXX_08_e11: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e11_001: I wonder if {SetColor=Gold}destroying{SetColor=Default} the piles of orichalcum will\nperhaps {SetColor=Gold}weaken the giant{SetColor=Default}?
MID_SCXX_08_e12: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e12_001: I shall confront the giant directly. You will all support\nme by destroying the orichalcum!
MID_SCXX_08_e15: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e15_001: <DLG>An orichalcum pile has been destroyed.\n\nNumber destroyed: {Variable=0}
MID_SCXX_08_e17: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e17_001: Well done! Destroy the remaining orichalcum!
MID_SCXX_08_e18: <TH>
MID_SCXX_08_e18_001: The orichalcum has been destroyed! Now, join\nLord Solel and bring down that giant!
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01: <EDH>
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_001: That was closer than I would have liked.\nIs everyone alright?
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_002: I'm fine, even though that was kinda rough.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_003: The idea of losing my life outside of battle\nis dismaying.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_004: That was a treacherous mission. I feel fortunate to\nhave escaped unharmed.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_005: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_006: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_007: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_008: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_009: *cough* *cough* I'm alright too. Thanks for asking.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_010: Now then, Vinicius. Let's hear your tale.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_011: Lord Solel, stay back! Something is off about\nthis man.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_012: Forgive your wretched servant...for failing to fulfill\nthe role given unto me...
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_013: For Magistra Raksha... I must take my own life...
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_014: Hrk... Urgh...
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_015: I cannot believe he'd stab himself in the throat.\nWhat inspired such zealotry?
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_016: Now that you mention it, I heard a concerning rumor\nwhile investigating the Order.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_017: Apparently a kiss from Magistra Raksha makes her\nminions incapable of defying her.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_018: Ensnared by a kiss, are they?
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_019: Hm. To insist on death for those who fail her is\nruthless indeed.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_076: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_020: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_021: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_022: Raksha's kiss? I, too, have received it.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_023: Yet I have not noticed any effect.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_024: I guess the cache is buried under all that rubble now.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_025: On the bright side, the cave-in eliminated all trace\nof our presence as well.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_026: I doubt even the Order of Mithras could excavate\nthat orichalcum in secret now.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_027: Their true objectives remain unclear, but this ought\nto slow their plans a bit.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_028: I'd call that a successful mission!
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_029: All's well that ends well! Now isn't it time we\ngot home?
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_030: Hold, Anna. Let me see what you have hidden in\nyour pockets.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_031: Awww... *sigh*
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_032: I'm impressed you had time to swipe that, Anna.\nYou've got some guts.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_033: I...respect the tenacity it took to gather that amidst\nthe confusion.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_034: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_035: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_036: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_037: You must not be seen breaking the law, Anna.\nI'll go ahead and take these.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_038: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_039: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_040: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_077: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_078: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_079: 
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_041: Things may not have gone according to plan, but we\ncan take solace in what we learned of our enemy.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_042: Thank you for your support in this matter. I will see\nto it that your reward is delivered later.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_043: This is where we must part. Again, I urge you to\nspeak of today's events to no one.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_044: They're deeper into the empire than we thought.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_045: If even Vinicius was taken in, I honestly don't know\nif there's anyone in the temples we can trust.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_046: Magistra Raksha is a more dangerous foe than I gave\nher credit for.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_047: We'll need to be even more cautious with our\ninvestigation going forward.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_048: What do you think the Order of Mithras wants with\nthis much orichalcum?
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_049: Hmm.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_050: I can hazard a guess.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_051: Back in 932, something unforeseen happened when\na certain person was executed in Dagda's cauldron.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_052: It was said that an unknown force extended from\nwithin and damaged the cauldron severely.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_053: According to witnesses, that unknown force was\nlike a spreading darkness.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_054: Darkness? What do you think it was?
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_055: I have heard of a very rare few among the People of\nthe White Egg with special hearts.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_056: The cauldron's destruction may have been caused by\ncasting one such person into it.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_057: At any rate, my father was clearly unstable after that.\nPerhaps he feared losing access to flamma.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_058: The first thing he did was to order Magistra Raksha\nto repair the cauldron immediately.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_059: Those repairs were estimated to require a vast\namount of orichalcum—50 years' worth of mining.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_060: But at the Divine Emperor's command, the necessary\norichalcum was sent to Dagsion.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_061: But if that's true, wouldn't Dagda's cauldron already\nbe fixed?
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_062: Eight years after that incident, Father entered his\nlong slumber. I became Divine Sovereign in his stead.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_063: I put a stop to Magistra Raksha's repairs and secured\nthe cauldron underground.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_064: By my decree, the remaining orichalcum was used to\ncreate Arcs instead.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_065: So you think Magistra Raksha may be plotting to\npick up where the repairs left off?
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_066: Maybe she hopes to have it done for the Divine\nEmperor's awakening after the Heroic Games.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_067: But this makes no sense...
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_068: Even if the heavens and earth turned upside down,\nthere's no coming back from that.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_069: What does she know that I don't?
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_070: Lord Solel? Is everything alright?
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_071: It's nothing.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_072: Repairing the cauldron was Dagda the Great's direct\norder to Magistra Raksha.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_073: We could question her about these suspicious goings-\non, but she has that to fall back on as a pretext.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_074: We must discover their true aims...no matter how\ndeep they run.
MID_SCXX_08_03_m01_075: There is no doubt that something sinister is stirring\nin the shadows of the Dagdan Empire...